sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-teissieri-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-teissieri-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-teissieri-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Drosophila teissieri Turing wavelength at 1.7 µm (detail scale s0, Holocene 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 86.2/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Schnakenberg kinetics on a periodic 20.64 µm patch with diffusivities solved so Turing's formula gives λ_c = 1.72 µm. Dispersion Pearson r = 0.9935 (RMSE 0.030 1/s) on the real-eigenvalue band. Equal-diffusion and autocatalysis-ablation controls both decay. A six-point diffusivity sweep is monotonic in the analytical wavelength (numerical Pearson r = 0.9995). The saturated sub-bin wavelength is 1.903 µm, 10.6% longer than the formula wavelength: the growth-rate peak is not the determinant minimizer, and that comparison is not yet a scored measurement (R1). Specimen CV similarity of the 12-frame 800×600 GIF is 88.4. The KS statistic (0.450) compares the raw activator to the micrograph, not the rendered frame the fitness test sees (R2). Overall 86.2/100 (faithfulness 85.6, reproducibility 87.6); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 82, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 84, Source and data traceability 86, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_teissieri_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-teissieri-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 475296 B, 1512×984 px, artifact_sha256 3afee39d65af76a252cc08a982ab25bf93da7d9e7f64ba49f32fe573813cd6dd (sha256 3afee39d65af76a252cc08a982ab25bf93da7d9e7f64ba49f32fe573813cd6dd), spec_fingerprint eae547f9e47b2ea29de70862c97589eafea17d3c75744f5144aa5ef1d4f3d6d0. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: eae547f9e47b2ea29de70862c97589eafea17d3c75744f5144aa5ef1d4f3d6d0; artifact_sha256: 3afee39d65af76a252cc08a982ab25bf93da7d9e7f64ba49f32fe573813cd6dd. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 critical wavenumber and the unequal-diffusivity condition. | Schnakenberg 1979 reaction terms a - u + u^2 v and b - u^2 v. | Tsacas 1971 name Drosophila teissieri, confirmed at GBIF 5074619. Tamura 2003 dates the melanogaster-subgroup radiation.; reconstructed_in_script: (a, b, gamma, Dv/Du) = (0.13, 0.91, 1.15, 17.4) so the formula wavelength is 1.72 µm. | Explicit Euler, linearised dispersion check, magnified inset on the vendored micrograph.; transfer_boundary: 1.72 µm is the campaign detail-scale assignment, not a published teissieri granule measurement. | Predecessor 97.6 µm and successor floor 2.72 µm are atlas contrasts at 0 Ma, not an ancestor-descendant series.; does_not_claim: That a wet-lab paper measured 1.72 µm on D. teissieri. | That D. virilis descends from D. teissieri. | That DOI 10.1093/molbev/msx210 is about this species (Crossref: yeast de-novo genes).." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "open need [morphometric_validation/morphometric-validation, pressure P=3.0]: Compare saturated wavelength to the σ(k) peak and KS the rendered frame against the specimen.",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Saturated sub-bin wavelength is 1.903 µm versus formula λ_c = 1.72 µm. Score the growth-rate peak explicitly and report how close the selected mode is to that peak, not only to the determinant minimizer.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'KS (0.450) compares the raw activator histogram to the micrograph. Add a KS between the rendered last GIF frame and the specimen, which is the image the fitness test scores.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Single builder-assessor. Gallery micrograph is a fallback (no Commons bitmap), so specimen-match cannot rise to a verified species photograph.'}" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.862"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single agent; no second provider on this pass)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://x.ai> .
}

